      en: ["Dingač became the first internationally protected wine region in Croatia in 1961.", "The vineyard slopes reach a steepness of up to 45 degrees.", "The primary grape variety cultivated is the indigenous Plavac Mali.", "The 400-meter-long Dingač tunnel was constructed in 1973 for access.", "The vines receive sun radiation from three sources: sky, sea, and rock.", "Harvesting is entirely manual due to the inaccessible terrain."],
